- `branch(b1, AND)`, `precedence(b1, n2)`, `precedence(b1, n3)`, `precedence(b1, n4)`, `precedence(b1, n5)`: Models "SAP Configuration", "Communications Design", "Learning Design", and "Data Conversion Design & Test" as parallel activities, contradicting the source text which explicitly sequences them ("followed by SAP Configuration. After that, it moves on to Communications Design. Then, it proceeds to Learning Design. Next, it involves Data Conversion Design & Test.").
- Missing `precedence(n2, n3)`, `precedence(n3, n4)`, `precedence(n4, n5)`: Fails to preserve the strict chronological order stated in the source due to the incorrect parallel split at `b1`.
- `action(n12, "End")`, `precedence(n11, n12)`, `precedence(n12, e1)`: Hallucinates a distinct "End" action step. The source only states the process ends after "PRODUCTION SUPPORT", requiring a direct link from `n11` to `e1`.
- `label(n5, c1, "following IT Design Development & Functional Test")`: Mislabels the path originating from "Data Conversion Design & Test" with an IT Design condition. Source specifies this track proceeds to Integration Test after Data Conversion, not IT Design.
- `label(n7, c2, "following Integration Test")`, `label(n8, c2, "following Integration Test")`, `label(n9, c2, "following Integration Test")`: Incorrectly claims "Communications Deployment", "Learning Deployment", and "Integration Test" occur *after* Integration Test. Source indicates these three activities converge into "Deployment", not that they follow Integration Test chronologically.